{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/l4bitgn6","slide":9,"bbox":[878,311,351,0]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/m5kjmlor","slide":9,"text":"A randomized trial found that phone alerts increased CPR started by nearby trained volunteers before EMS arrival.","textPreview":"A randomized trial found that phone alerts increased CPR started by nearby trained volunteers before EMS arrival.","textChars":113,"textLines":1,"bbox":[878,337,351,166]}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/n6d0vq5c","slide":9,"bbox":[69,537,1138,92]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/jadgjqlk","slide":9,"text":"Project contribution: a prototype that places map context, emergency content and AI interaction in one mobile journey.","textPreview":"Project contribution: a prototype that places map context, emergency content and AI interaction in one mobile journey.","textChars":118,"textLines":1,"bbox":[95,549,1080,72]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/i94zal4z","slide":9,"text":"Sources: WHO emergency care; 112 India; Ringh et al., NEJM (2015)","textPreview":"Sources: WHO emergency care; 112 India; Ringh et al., NEJM (2015)","textChars":65,"textLines":1,"bbox":[72,647,1100,25]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gfyxx2","slide":9,"text":"[1] WHO, Emergency care, https://www.who.int/health-topics/emergency-care\n[2] Government of India, Emergency Response Support System, https://112.gov.in/\n[3] M. Ringh et al., Mobile-Phone Dispatch of Laypersons for CPR in Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest, New England Journal of Medicine 372 (2015), 2316–2325, https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa1406038 . The project contribution is a prototype integration and research direction, not a measured improvement over existing systems. 112 India also offers a SHOUT volunteer feature for women and children."}
